# BinFlow M10 tier matrix contract baseline (T-277, ADR-0032/0033 / architecture 15.6).
# RE-FROZEN by T-283 (ADR-0032 / architecture 15.5 is the registering ADR): the
# addons.disabled config key the ADR carries makes the disabled form BOOTABLE,
# flipping its six BOOTFAIL cells to the real posture (npm=400 under the
# breaker, generic=200, the gated pilots 400 at the community floor). The same
# re-freeze absorbs the T-279 (T01) and T-282 (T02) whitelist flips into the
# baseline — their entries left the whitelist registry (absorbed, not
# withdrawn). T05/T06 stay 400 on every form while the license forms run
# UN-INSTALLED (no --license-dir documents; the stock binary's embedded verify
# key has no signer by design) — the pro-tier 2xx premise is proven by the
# constructor-injection legs in internal/httpapi/t283_gate_test.go
# (TestT283CreateGateD3), not by this matrix, until T-281's keygen lands.
# Frozen: commit e32c63f, 2026-08-25T14:24:38Z, from ephemeral instances
# (the script's default boot mode; license forms recorded in their un-installed
# posture until --license-dir carries T-281 keygen output).
# Recorded by: scripts/m10-tier-matrix.sh --record [--force] (default form set).
